    },
    {
      "turn_id": 2,
      "parent_turn_id": 1,
      "role": "user",
      "content_blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Compare them. More context: most writes come from the orders and billing services, tenant metadata is relatively small, and the audit_log table is huge but not latency sensitive. We also have a handful of sequences that external systems assume are monotonic, though not gapless. Our app is mostly Ruby and Go, with some jobs that hit the DB directly using SQL. I keep hearing three options from the team: native logical replication, a managed migration service with ongoing replication, or some kind of blue-green approach with short read-only mode at the end. I am worried about DDL drift, long-running transactions, and the fact that some reporting queries still do full table scans on old partitions.",
